{
  "$comment": [
    "Search-grammar conformance corpus (DUP-8). The Ctrl-K query dialect is",
    "implemented twice -- crates/tine-core/src/search_query.rs for the block list",
    "and src/editor/searchQuery.ts for the page list -- and the two files only ask",
    "each other, in prose, to stay in sync. This corpus is the executable version of",
    "that request: every case is asserted by a Rust test against `tokenize` /",
    "`Matcher::parse` and by a vitest test against `tokenize` / `parseSearchQuery`.",
    "It pins CURRENT behavior. A row here is not an endorsement -- it is a record of",
    "what both engines do today, so that a change to one of them shows up as a",
    "failing diff instead of as a query that filters differently depending on which",
    "list you are looking at.",
    "A case has either a shared `tokens`/`verdict` (both engines agree) or a",
    "`knownDivergence` with per-engine `rust`/`typescript` sections. The divergent",
    "rows are DUP-9 findings; neither tokenizer was changed to make them agree.",
    "`verdict.kind: \"invalid\"` carries no message: the two regex engines word their",
    "errors differently and that difference is not a contract."
  ],
